      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Cannot intentionally reproduce however it seems to happen in larger lobbies for new joiners (chance improves when the player and their avatar is not loaded in cache).\n\nNotable side effects is nameplates and chatboxes become detached from the player separately, with nameplates sometimes moving around teleporting to the player while the chatbox stays in place, usually near spawn and continues to follow the rule of being near proximity allows them to be visible.\n\nNeither the chatbox nor the nameplate will billboard-rotate and stay facing the one direction.\n\nThis was in the great pug, where the chatbox seems to be 10x larger than the map itself.\n\nUsing an alt account, I was able to trigger the bug and took it to the moon with me to see the scale of the chatbox in question.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
